  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In 2003, a former CIA officer named Rolf Mowatt-Larssen says he spent a weekend at the White House with Vice President Dick Cheney, talking through why the Iraq war was being lost. Mowatt-Larssen tells Michels this as someone who was there, saying he got to know Cheney \"exceptionally well\", and he points to his own book, A State of Mind: Faith and the CIA. It places him in the inner circle of the war's planning at the highest level."
